        },
        {
          "amendment_id": "fr-1-15dd3c0b",
          "source_stage": "final_review",
          "source_cycle": 2,
          "source_completion_round": 1,
          "body": "The `substrate_root_activity_factor` computation at substrate.rs:348 uses `(surface_area_cm2 - footprint_area_cm2).max(0.0)` to isolate interstitial area. This is correct when SubstrateSurface = footprint + interstitial, but if the habitat registry formula ever changes, this subtraction will silently produce wrong results. Add an inline comment explaining the physical meaning: 'SubstrateSurface area includes footprint top surface; subtract it to get only interstitial grain-matrix area available for root colonization.'",
